Repro: 1. Create a project and switch to View > LaTeX. 2. At the end of the body, before \end{document}, add these lines without blank lines between the paragraph and the commands:
ZXTIGHT paragraph before a section
\section{ZXTIGHT SECTION}
ZXTIGHT section body
\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\begin{tabular}{ll}
ZXTIGHT & 9 \\
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
3. Click 'Apply source', then View > Visual, then View > LaTeX.
Actual: Apply reports success (`Visual document synchronized from LaTeX.`), but the visual document has no ZXTIGHT SECTION heading and no table; it shows the literal text `\section{ZXTIGHT SECTION}`, `\begin{table}`, `\begin{tabular}` and `\end{tabular}`. Returning to the source shows the commands rewritten as `\textbackslash{}section\{ZXTIGHT SECTION\}`, `\textbackslash{}begin\{table\}`, etc., so the LaTeX is permanently corrupted as well. The same failure occurs for a \section command alone without the table, so any block command that is not preceded by a blank line is affected.
